    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nOPEN VIEWING Tuesday the 29th, 4:30pm-5pm. No. 37 St Gabriel's is a superbly presented family home positioned within this highly regarded and mature development in the heart of Cabinteely, Dublin 18. Built by Shannon Homes in 1999 on the historic grounds of the former St Gabriel's Hospital, St Gabriels is admired for its attractive layout, generous green spaces and established setting. This remarkable property offers luxurious family living of the highest calibre. \n\nBeautifully extended and upgraded by its current owners, No. 37 offers stylish contemporary accommodation finished to an exceptional standard throughout. The accommodation extends across generously scaled living and bedroom spaces, perfectly suited to modern family life and elegant entertaining alike. \n\nAt the heart of the home is a stunning open-plan kitchen/dining, living space which has been thoughtfully designed to create a wonderful hub for both everyday family living and entertaining. The home impresses with its high ceilings and large windows giving an abundance of natural light, creating a wonderful sense of space throughout. The luxurious bathrooms, are all updated and finished to an exceptional standard, incorporating premium fittings. Every detail has been carefully curated, with refined interior design finishes and beautifully appointed reception rooms that balance comfort with understated luxury. \n\nOriginally designed as a four-bedroom home, the property has been cleverly reconfigured by the current owners to create a luxurious principal suite by combining two bedrooms, complete with a beautifully appointed ensuite. There are two further bedrooms at this level, one large double with an ensuite, a single bedroom with ample storage, while the attic has been converted to provide an additional room currently used as a bedroom, adding excellent versatility to the accommodation. The attic also has a contemporary spacious shower room and velux windows. \n\nTo the rear, the landscaped garden provides a private outdoor sanctuary. Designed for both relaxation and entertaining, it features mature manicured buxus hedging and olive trees, creating a wonderfully private and tranquil outdoor space.\n\n37 St Gabriels represents a rare opportunity to acquire a truly distinguished home in one of South Dublin's most sought-after residential locations, where exclusivity, design excellence and luxurious living come together seamlessly."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Special Features</li><li> Highly sought-after residential location within the mature St Gabriel's development in Cabinteely</li><li> Built by Shannon Homes and designed by architects McCrossan O'Rourke</li><li> Extended family home with well-balanced and spacious accommodation totalling c175 sqm</li><li> Stunning open-plan kitchen/dining/family room forming the heart of the home with double doors to the rear garden</li><li> Vaulted ceiling in the extension creating a wonderful sense of space and light</li><li> Fully fitted kitchen with high-end finishes and BOSCH appliances</li><li> Elegant main reception room with open fireplace</li><li> Guest WC at ground floor level</li><li> Converted attic room currently used as an additional bedroom</li><li> Gas-fired central heating</li><li> Double glazed windows throughout</li><li> Private driveway offering ample parking</li><li> Sunny southerly aspect to the rear garden</li><li> Beautifully maintained communal green areas within the development</li><li> Walking distance to Cabinteely park and village with its shops, cafés and amenities</li><li> Close to a wide selection of excellent primary and secondary schools</li><li> Excellent transport links; offering easy access to the M50 and the N11, serviced by Dublin Bus QBC with excellent public transport links into the city centre. Both the Luas and the Dart are a 10 minute drive.</ul>"
      },
